              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, suppose that the Georgia Supreme Court in this case had issued an order saying we affirm the decision below; our decision should not be taken as necessarily agreeing or disagreeing with the reasoning in the lower court's opinion. Would look-through be appropriate in that situation?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, you can't say?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, suppose -- suppose that there is a decision by a state intermediate court of appeals, and the majority rejects a claim for certain reasons, and there's a concurrence in the judgment that says we would also reject the claim -- or I would also reject the claim for a different reason, and then that decision is summarily affirmed by the state supreme court. What happens there?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, at what point does it become, would you say, okay, well, that's enough, it's reasonable?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, now, Richter does require a habeas court, a federal habeas court to imagine all of the conceivable arguments that could have supported a state court decision, correct?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 32,
              "start": 32
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, I'm not sure I understand the question. But suppose you said that the reasoned decision is -- is not -- is just completely wrong."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, all right? Could the state come in with a totally new argument that wasn't made to the state court at all and say you should deny habeas on this totally new argument?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, so why do we bother having state habeas anymore? Why don't we just say don't -- have federal habeas only and -"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, where is the question of -- of Georgia law that is implicated here?"
      }
    ],
